    "https://uottawa.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/uOttawa_External_Career_Site/job/Main-Campus/ATPUO---Winter-2027---MBA5280B00----Operations---Supply-Chain-Management_JR38504": {
      "title": "ATPUO - Winter 2027 - MBA5280B00 - \tOperations & Supply Chain Management",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-18\nPosted: Posted 22 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPosting Reason: New Position Location: Ottawa, ON Academic Period: 2027 Winter Semester Faculty: École de gestion Telfer / Telfer School of Management Academic Unit: Telfer School of Management Course Title: Operations & Supply Chain Management Course Code: MBA5280 Section: B00 Course Description: Introduction to the nature of the supply chains and the elements that play a crucial role in their competitiveness. Specifically, how efficient, responsive, and agile supply chains are designed and managed in terms of the internal operations of the involved organizations; their sourcing, logistics, and customer demand management capabilities; as well as their integrated approach toward supply chain strategy and performance measurement. Emerging related topics such as lean supply chains and supply chain risks and resilience will also be discussed. Posting limited to: Professeur à temps-partiel régulier / Regular Part-Time Professor Date Posted (YYYY/MM/DD): 2026/08/18 Applications must be received BEFORE (YYYY/MM/DD): 2026/09/18 Expected Enrolment: 35 Approval date: 2026/08/18 Number of credits: 1.5 Work Hours: 19.5 Hourly Rate: Enseignement / Teaching: $239.47 (2024-2025) The academic year starts on September 1 and ends on August 31. These rates do not included vacation pay nor statutory pay. These rates will be applied until a new collective agreement is ratified. Retro will be paid after the ratification. Course type: D Posting type: Régulier / Regular Language of instruction: Anglais | English Competence in second language: Passive Course Schedule: - - - Saturdays, January 9, 23, February 6 & Sundays, January 10, 24, February 7 from 8:30 to 11:30am Requirements: Must have a Master's degree in an area directly related to the course and demonstrate related experience in the area of the course; or a Canadian baccalaureate degree or its international equivalent with a professional designa